  "holistic_F_N": -1,
  "holistic_F_H": 2,
  "section_notes": "S1 is strong, requiring all incidents reported within 24 hours and customer notice within 72 hours. S2 adopts a 55°C test and 5% permanent failure limit, gives exact per-model results to customers and regulators but bars public disclosure, and allows corrective action before withdrawal; S3 sets new-unit shut-off at 24 months and retrofit at 6 years, while S4 requires built-in suppression at 36 months. S5 keeps an 8/100k numeric trigger for regulator review/corrective action but makes recall mandatory only on a regulator finding of serious risk or failed corrective action, with prompt customer notices."
